        <dc:title>The Laws of Late Medieval Italy (1000–1500): Foundations for a European Legal System</dc:title>
        <dcterms:abstract>This book shows how the Italian legal system developed mainly thanks to the cooperation of universities. In this way a Continental 'common law' was built which even today is useful as a common heritage.</dcterms:abstract>
