        <dc:title>The problem of the Kingdom of Majorca (1229/76–1343) 1. Political identity</dc:title>
        <dcterms:abstract>This article examines the motives behind the creation of a Catalan kingdom of Majorca in 1276, comprising the Balearic islands, Roussillon, Cerdagne, Montpellier, and some other lands in what is now southern France. It is argued that the apparent diversity of territories has created an erroneous assumption that this kingdom had no real coherence. The relationship of each part to the whole is described, and the tension that developed between the Majorcan and the Aragonese kings is analysed.</dcterms:abstract>
        <dc:date>1990</dc:date>
        <z:language>English</z:language>
        <z:shortTitle>The problem of the Kingdom of Majorca</z:shortTitle>
        <bib:pages>150-168</bib:pages>
    </bib:Article>
