        <link:link rdf:resource="#item_39598"/>
        <dc:subject>Mediterranean</dc:subject>
        <dc:subject>Political History</dc:subject>
        <dc:subject>1200s</dc:subject>
        <dc:subject>Andalusia (Iberia)</dc:subject>
        <dc:title>Las actividades marítimas en Andalucía durante el reinado de Alfonso X</dc:title>
        <dcterms:abstract>This work studies the early stages of the planning and management of Andalusian coastal lands after the conquest. It connects many sectorial works, trying to find a global sense for the phenomenon”. It firstly analyses the policies for populating these áreas, whereby the new settlers were granted general and specific privileges. Secondly, it deals with articulation of territorial defence mechanisms, specially those concerning the creation and maintenance of fletes. Lastly, it considers those economic activities carried out with the aim of strengthening the settling down of these groups and enhancing the region’s commercial appeal.</dcterms:abstract>
        <dc:date>2020</dc:date>
        <z:language>Spanish</z:language>
        <bib:pages>182-210</bib:pages>
    </bib:Article>
